  "summary": "I wrote the solar-system explorer in `src/main.ts`, but none of it has run, and `@aura3d/engine` is not installed in this sandbox. Typecheck reports only `TS2307: Cannot find module '@aura3d/engine'`, so every Aura3D call is unchecked against the real types. `vite build` will also fail here until the package is installed. I wrote it only against the signatures in `docs/agents` and the recipe sources. Treat the first real build and a run in the browser as the actual test.\n\n**What it contains**\n- A glowing emissive star with bloom, a point light at its centre, and about 380 instanced emissive stars on a dark background.\n- Eight planets (Mercury to Neptune) with different sizes, colours and orbital distances. Inner planets orbit faster, with period scaled as the square root of the real period (Mercury 8 s, Neptune about 209 s).\n- Each planet has a thin orbit line, spins on its axis, and carries spots and bands so the spin is visible. Earth has one moon and Jupiter has two. Saturn has a two-band ring.\n- The star, planets, rings and moons are primitives and custom geometry. The orbit lines are a custom line-topology mesh. Nothing is loaded from the network.\n- Clicking a planet, `window.__focusPlanet(name)`, Escape, a click on empty space and `window.__unfocus()` all go through the same focus and unfocus functions.\n- The camera takes 1.5 s with cubic easing to a close view of the planet on its lit side. It keeps following the planet as it orbits, and it also returns to the overview in 1.5 s.\n- A DOM panel shows the planet's name, orbital period in Earth days and distance from the star in million km.\n- In the overview, dragging orbits the camera and the wheel zooms between 60 and 300 units.\n- The Pause/Play button stops orbits, spins and moons. Camera moves keep running while paused.\n- `window.__TASK_STATE__` is a read-only getter returning a frozen snapshot with `ready`, `focused`, `paused`, `planets` and `cameraDistanceToFocus`. `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after two a",
